# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docker build context allow-list-by-exclusion.
#
# Why this file exists: the Dockerfile runs `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`
# and THEN `COPY . .`. Without these rules a local `docker build .` (or any
# context that is not a clean git clone) drops the host's macOS `node_modules`
# on top of the Linux tree the image just installed — native binaries mismatch,
# the standalone output is silently broken — and pushes ~8 GB of context to the
# daemon. `.env` is excluded for the same reason it is git-ignored: the runtime
# config belongs to the K8s ConfigMap, never to the image.
#
# CI/CD note: Jenkins clones a fresh checkout, so most of these are already
# absent there; this file makes the image reproducible for local builds too.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# dependencies / build output (regenerated inside the builder stage)
node_modules
.next
out
build
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo

# host-only runtime config — injected per environment by K8s
.env
.env.*

# reports, scratch dirs and logs (never part of the app)
upload
test
prompt
skills
*.log
dev.log
server.log

# local tooling / agent artifacts
.git
.github
.DS_Store
.claude
.arts/
.codeartsdoer/
.merkle-snapshot.json
*.pid
*.pem

# process managers & editor/CI files not needed inside the image
logs
pidfile
pid
.pm2
